{{Quote|Two more X-wings down. That's half our fleet destroyed!|Dand reports the loss of two more Resistance fighters|<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref>}}
'''Vober Dand''' was a [[Tarsunt]] [[Gender|male]]<ref name="TFAVD" /> from [[Suntilla]]<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> who served in the [[Resistance]]'s [[Ground Logistics Division]] as a [[controller]]. Around thirty [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Endor]],<ref name="TFAVD" /> he was stationed in the Resistance's [[Resistance base|base of operations]] on the [[planet]] [[D'Qar]] and was present during the preparations and execution of the Resistance's [[Battle of Starkiller Base|attack]] on the [[First Order]]'s [[Starkiller Base]].<ref name="TFA" />

During the [[Battle of D'Qar|evacuation of D'Qar]], Dand was stationed on the Resistance [[flagship]], [[Raddus (MC85 Star Cruiser)|''Raddus'']]. Whilst aboard the vessel Dand argued with [[Captain]] [[Poe Dameron]] about the best way they could reshuffle the fleet's remaining starfighters to defend the ship.<ref name="Expanded Edition">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> He was later present when [[Vice Admiral]] [[Amilyn Holdo]] was given command of the Resistance, and listened to her introductory speech.<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>

Dand was left as one of the few Resistance members to survive the [[Battle of Crait]] and started working with his [[Parent|father]], [[Ibdun Dand]], who had joined after the [[Hosnian Cataclysm]], as part of the [[Resistance ground crew|ground crew]] of the [[Resistance base (Ajan Kloss)|Resistance base]] on [[Ajan Kloss]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> in [[35 ABY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref>

After the Resistance and its [[Citizens' Fleet|allies]] defeated the [[Sith Eternal military|Sith Eternal forces]] at the [[battle of Exegol]], Dand celebrated with his father at the Resistance base along with the [[Kessurian]] [[Wilsa Teshlo]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
Dand was a stickler for detail and refused to tolerate anyone operating outside of protocol. He wore a [[Color|yellow]] GLD controller's coat with "GLD Landing Officer" printed on it in [[Aurebesh]] lettering. He also wore a pair of brown pants and [[boot]]s as well as a [[comlink]] headset. Dand had brown [[hair]], black [[eye]]s and gray skin.<ref name="TFAVD" />

==Behind the scenes==
Vober Dand first appeared in the film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']] which was released in [[2015]].<ref name="TFA" /> He was not identified in the film, but received a name in ''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]] and released the same day as the film.<ref name="TFAVD" /> He was portrayed by [[Derek Arnold]] in the film, but was not listed in the end credits.<ref name="Arnold">{{WebCite|url=https://starwarsinterviews.com/sequel-trilogy/episode-vii-the-force-awakens/derek-arnold-vober-dand|text=Derek Arnold (Vober Dand)|author=[[Dennis Pellegrom]]|date=2016-04|work=[[Star Wars Interviews]]|archivedate=20230205201458|nolive=1}}</ref>

